] [17592186097292 #edb/ref 1069 "q-50029" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097292 #edb/ref 1071 "A cat’s position relative to a fixed origin $O$ is given by the function $x(t) = 3t^{2} + t$ meters, where $t$ is the time in hours. Find the average position of the cat between $2$ and $4$ hours.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097292 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "06277fd5-c6be-5879-81ac-2b86cefe4004" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097292 #edb/ref 1073 true #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097294 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186095688 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097294 #edb/ref 1069 "q-50036" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097294 #edb/ref 1071 "A train is moving north-east with velocity $v(t) = 6t^{2} + 8t + 100km/h$, where $t$ is the time in hours. Find the average velocity of the train on the interval $t ∈ [1, 4]$.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097294 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e6f31648-32f5-5f87-b9bb-fc4d6a7438c9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097294 #edb/ref 1073 true #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097588 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186097589 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097588 #edb/ref 1061 2011 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097588 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "defa2861-ea0b-5be8-a72a-4101e1177359" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097588 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186097791 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097589 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186097590 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097589 #edb/ref 1061 2012 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097589 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "c2c3e774-0466-5687-8348-ec20933d1013" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097589 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186096717 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097590 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186097591 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097590 #edb/ref 1061 2014 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097590 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "9c935206-0fc0-512a-9bf5-4f346bee6bcf" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097590 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186096718 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097591 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186097592 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097591 #edb/ref 1061 2016 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097591 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "12ea46a3-a7a9-5273-ae68-f843dba89bf3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097591 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186097792 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097592 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186097676 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097592 #edb/ref 1061 2017 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097592 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "7fa5d198-6f76-58fe-a0de-a2eede2c04f2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097592 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186096719 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097593 #edb/ref 1061 2019 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097593 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "63d935f4-c3b0-5692-aa00-a8d6bc7db985" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097593 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186096720 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097676 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186097593 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097676 #edb/ref 1061 32551 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097676 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "4f5e263b-c885-5894-bec5-5d0237b91689" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097676 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186097881 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097791 #edb/ref 1064 "For a particle with position $x(t)$, the **average velocity** of the particle over the time interval $[a,b]$ is given by the average rate of change of position:\n\n$$\nv_{\\textrm{avg}} = \\dfrac{\\Delta x}{\\Delta t} = \\dfrac{x(b) - x(a)}{b-a}\n$$\n\nSimilarly, the **average acceleration** of a particle with velocity $v(t)$ over the time interval $[a,b]$ is given by the average rate of change of velocity:\n\n$$\na_{\\textrm{avg}} = \\dfrac{\\Delta v}{\\Delta t} = \\dfrac{v(b) - v(a)}{b-a}\n$$\n\nTo demonstrate, suppose that a particle moves along a straight line, and its position (in meters) relative to a fixed origin $O$ is given by the function\n\n$$\nx(t) = 2t^3\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nt \\geq 0\n$$\n\nis the time measured in seconds. The average velocity of the particle over the time interval $[0,1]$ is\n\n$$\nv_{avg} = \\frac{Δx}{Δt} = (x(1) - x(0))/(1 - 0) = (2(1)^{3} - 2(0)^{3})/(1 - 0) = 2m/s\n$$\n\nLikewise, the velocity is\n\n$$\nv(t) = x'(t) = 6t^2\n$$\n\nso the average acceleration of the particle over the time interval $[0,1]$ is\n\n$$\na_{avg} = \\frac{Δv}{Δt} = (v(1) - v(0))/(1 - 0) = (6(1)^{2} - 6(0)^{2})/(1 - 0) = 6m/s^{2}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097791 #edb/ref 1065 1023 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097791 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "e1c49e4b-7206-5819-b127-c2f562fa1043" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097791 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097792 #edb/ref 1064 "So, we now know how to find\n\n- the average *velocity* (given the *position*), and\n- the average *acceleration* (given the *velocity*).\n\nBut what if we are given the *velocity* and asked to find the average *velocity*? That's a bit trickier. However, we can solve this problem by recalling that the average value of a function $v(t)$ over the interval $[t_1,t_2]$ is given by\n\n$$\nv_{\\textrm{avg}} = \\dfrac{1}{t_2-t_1}\\int_{t_1}^{t_2} v(t)\\,\\textrm d t\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097792 #edb/ref 1065 1026 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097792 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "b25ff39d-cfec-5109-8c49-31a8d54ad75d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097792 #edb/ref 1067 "Calculating Average Velocity Using Integration" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097881 #edb/ref 1064 "We can also calculate the average position $x_{\\textrm{avg}}$ and average acceleration $a_{\\textrm{avg}}$ of a particle over an interval $[t_1, t_2]$ using the following formulas:\n\n$$\nx_{avg} = \\frac{1}{t_{2} - t_{1}}\\int_{t_{1}}^{t_{2}}x(t)dt; a_{avg} = \\frac{1}{t_{2} - t_{1}}\\int_{t_{1}}^{t_{2}}a(t)dt\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097881 #edb/ref 1065 5192 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097881 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "8e1cdc1f-de87-5b91-9ad0-f2bcab98be3f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097881 #edb/ref 1067 "Calculating Average Position and Acceleration Using Integration" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
